      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L02-ACTIVITY-013",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: Cube It",
      "SourceExcerpt": "If a square has side length \\(s\\), then the area is \\(s^2\\). If a square has area \\(A\\), then the side length is \\(\\sqrt{A}\\). For a positive number \\(b\\), the square root of \\(b\\) is defined as the positive number that squares to make…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L02-ACTIVITY-014",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: Cube It",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Similarly, if a cube has edge length \\(s\\), then the volume is \\(s^3\\). If a cube has volume \\(V\\), then the edge length is \\(\\sqrt[3]{V}\\). The number \\(\\sqrt[3]{a}\\) is defined as the number that cubes to make \\(a\\). In other words,…",
